        "original_id": "d07ca6f5-3128-54b9-88d7-c5e6d077e49f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Podocarpus, Osmunda\n- Animals: Golden-plumed parakeet\n- Plant families: Podocarpaceae\n- Places: Colombia, Ecuador, Peru, east Andean slope\n- Habitats: Humid temperate highland forests\n\nFacts:\n- Podocarpus is a genus of conifers in the podocarp family, Podocarpaceae.\n- Podocarpus is the most numerous and widely distributed genus in Podocarpaceae.\n- Podocarpus plants are evergreen shrubs or trees, usually 1 to tall, and can reach 40 m.\n- Podocarpus includes approximately 97 to 107 species, depending on species circumscription.\n- Osmunda has had five to ten species listed for the genus.\n- The golden-plumed parakeet is found in humid temperate highland forests, especially forests with Podocarpus, on the east Andean slope in Colombia, Ecuador, and Peru.",
